course: dictionary
lesson: 11112
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word whisker is a good example. «Cat whiskers are thick, deep-rooted hairs that help a cat judge whether it can fit through a gap.» Here a whisker is one of the long stiff hairs on an animal.
explain: Now look at this: «She won the race by a whisker.» Nobody won a race with hairs on their face. Read the words around it: won and race tell you this is about winning, so by a whisker must mean by a tiny amount, only just.
explain: Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right one.
fact: A whisker is one of the long stiff hairs near the mouth of a cat, a mouse, a seal or many other animals.
fact: Animal whiskers are used to feel things, and they help a cat judge if it can fit through a gap.
fact: «By a whisker» means only just, by a tiny amount.
fact: «Whiskers» can also mean the hair growing on a man's face.
fact: «The cat's whiskers» is an old-fashioned phrase meaning the very best.
exercise: «Cat whiskers help a cat judge whether it can fit through a gap.» What do cat whiskers help a cat do? | Keep its tail warm | *Judge whether it can fit through a gap | Hear sounds far away | Make its fur shine
exercise: «She won the race by a whisker.» What does by a whisker mean? | Without running at all | *Only just | Covered in fur | Very far ahead of everyone
exercise: «Mice sweep their whiskers back and forth to feel the shape of things around them.» Find and copy the word that tells you what the whiskers are used for. | *feel | around | sweep | mice
test: «The walrus finds clams with its whiskers.» What do the walrus's whiskers help it do? | Cut through the sea | *Find clams | Climb onto the ice | Show its strength
test: Grandad says, «That new bike is the cat's whiskers!» What does he mean? | It has whiskers painted on it | It is very dirty | *It is the very best | It is only for cats
exam: Which phrase means only just, by a tiny amount? | *by a whisker | whiskers in the dark | the cat's whiskers | hair on a seal
